Error [E2302]: the `ref` field `name` would point at something that dies first
  --> tests/ui/ref_field_dangles_local.jet:7:30
    |
  7 |     val h: Holder = Holder { name: local };
    |                              ^^^^
 Why: a `ref` field stores a view, not its own copy, so its source has to outlive the struct — but the local `local` can live only as long as this function call
 Fix: store an owned value (drop `ref` and let the struct keep its own copy, or `.clone()` into it), or fill the `ref` from a parameter the caller keeps owning
